2026-08-25T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2013) 'Context and Problem Statement
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2013) 'The manuals repo now commits binary assets alongside prose, starting with screenshots under `decisions/attachments/`. Ad-hoc names like `image.png` collide, sort poorly, and lose their provenance once they leave the page that referenced them. What naming convention should committed assets follow so they stay unique, sortable, and self-describing?
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2013) 'Decision Drivers
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2013) '- Names should be unique and not collide across decisions.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2013) '- Names should sort chronologically and read as self-describing.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2013) '- Names should survive being copied out of the repo (provenance in the name).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2013) '- The convention should match established digital-preservation guidance.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2013) 'Considered Options
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2013) '- Keep source names (`image.png`, `screenshot (1).png`).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2013) '- Content hash names (`a1b2c3.png`).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2013) '- A Library of Congress style descriptive convention.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2013) 'Following the Library of Congress file-naming guidance
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2013) '- Lowercase ASCII only; no spaces or special characters.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2013) '- ISO 8601 date first (`YYYYMMDD`) so names sort chronologically.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2013) '- Facets separated by underscores (`_`); words within a facet by hyphens (`-`).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2013) '- A zero-padded sequence (`NNNN`) to keep same-day captures unique and ordered.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2013) '- Descriptive but reasonably short.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2013) 'Consequences
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2013) '- Good: assets are unique, sort by date, and carry their provenance in the name.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2013) '- Good: the convention matches preservation practice and is mechanical to apply.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2013) '- Bad: names are longer than source names, and renaming on import is a manual step.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2013) 'Confirmation
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2013) 'Assets under `decisions/attachments/` match `YYYYMMDD_project_description_NNNN.ext` and have a matching entry under `references:` in `CITATION.cff`. The first example is `20260606_vsekai-mpf_xr-grid-debug-orbs_0001.png`, cited from the presence-demo decision.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2013) 'More Information
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2013) 'Based on the Library of Congress guidance on file naming for digital preservation (descriptive, no spaces, lowercase, ISO dates, zero-padded sequences).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2013) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2013) 'What naming convention should committed assets follow so they stay unique, sortable, and self-describing?
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2013  1 LINE
 Text:Written
